Subject: [PATCH] browser page: Allow OAuth apps on Request VM
 (spec.oauthClients)

A field under Compute, one app per line (client_id, then scopes), maps to the
EphemeralInfra contract template's oauthClients and gives the contract a
secrets bundle, which carries /etc/socialweb-computer/oauth-wid.json to the VM.
The requester turns it into a com.fedproxy.rbac role the VM's workload identity
uses to approve those OAuth sign-ins as the signed-in account
(socialweb-computer-kcp plan 0040, docs/pds/oauth-wid.md). Needs an account on
a socialweb-computer PDS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XtTWStqstmFZHUkRsRsthA
